# Walkthrough: Firebase Cloud Synchronization

I've successfully integrated **Firebase Firestore** into your application to provide reliable, persistent cloud storage. This prevents data loss when your browser cache is cleared.

## Changes Made

1.  **Firebase SDK Integration**: Added `firebase` as a dependency and created [firebase.ts](file:///c:/Users/SONU%20MAHTO/Downloads/sonu-ice-cream-shop%20%281%29/firebase.ts) for initialization.
2.  **Modern Sync UI**: Replaced the broken Google Drive panel with a sleek Firebase Sync panel in the **Manage → Cloud** tab.
3.  **Auto-Sync Feature**: Added a "Set and Forget" auto-sync toggle that automatically backups your data every 5 seconds after a change.
4.  **Flexible Configuration**: You can now paste your Firebase Web Config directly into the app UI.

## How to Set Up (One-Time Setup)

To enable cloud sync, follow these simple steps:

1.  Go to the [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/).
2.  Create a project named **"Sonu Ice Cream"**.
3.  In the left sidebar, go to **Build → Firestore Database** and click **Create database**.
4.  Choose **"Start in test mode"** and select a location close to you.
5.  Go to **Project Settings** (gear icon) → **General**.
6.  Scroll down to "Your apps", click the **Web icon (</>)**, and register your app.
7.  Copy the `firebaseConfig` object (the part inside the `{ ... }`).
8.  Open your app, go to **Manage → Cloud**, paste the config, and click **Save Configuration**.

## How to Use

### Manual Backup/Restore
- **Upload**: Click the orange **Upload** button to force a backup of your current local data to the cloud.
- **Download**: Click **Download** to restore your data from the cloud. This will overwrite whatever is currently in your browser.

### Auto-Sync (Recommended)
- Toggle **Auto-Sync** to **ON**.
- The app will now automatically save your data to the cloud whenever you make a change (with a 5-second delay to save battery/data).
- You'll see a spinning icon when sync is in progress.

---

> [!TIP]
> **Pro Tip**: Even if you reset your browser or switch devices, just log in with the same username, paste your Firebase config, and click **Download** to get all your records back instantly!

